ram of RNA  polymerase 2 and what this enzyme does  this protein does is it attaches to the  viroid and it starts making copies of it  it takes RNA nucleotides that the cells  produced and it uses those nucleotides  to make copies  of the viroid and it does this over and  over and over again thousands and  thousands and thousands of copies of the  vibrator made this way and that is how  viroids make a living they steal a  protein from a plant cell and they spill  nucleotides from a plant cell and they  just make copies of themselves so there  you have it  viroids they are the simplest known  creatures on planet Earth  in fact they are the simplest known  creatures and all of the cosmos next  question

